Effect: seven miners mined beside a pirate pack; no ship lost, every run paid its 5,000 cr once.
Cause: the stop reads route.place or route.belt of mine and hunt routes; a circuit's stops are not read. I took the closure on Intel's word and did not read the stop's code.
Fix, done: the route set status off for danger with its reason (commit b3253bdd); asked of Unity: the pirate stop reads every system a circuit's stops name (requests.log, this turn). My skill mining-chains says to read the sightings for a circuit's mine stops until then.
Would it have prevented this one: the status off, from now on for this route; the stop on circuit stops, for every circuit of every division.

