## [ENT-119] | 2026-11-22 00:28 UTC | Apollo | error | ref: game/routes/guidebook/logistics/routes.md
Class: work left uncommitted in the shared clone (one member's commit held by another member's files in progress).
Case: 2026-11-22 00:16 UTC, my edit of the guidebook's Standing Plan (routes.md) was refused at commit by the pre-commit route check: seven untracked hunt route files of another member made master-index.md and index-standing-work.md stale. At 00:20 UTC the file no longer held my edit and git showed no change.
Effect: one guidebook entry lost for six minutes; written again from my draft and committed (948e8167). Nothing else lost.
Cause: the check judges the whole tree, not the staged paths, so a member's commit waits on another's work; who or what reverted the file is not found.
Fix, done: my skill logistics-stock says to commit an edit in the clone at once and keep its draft in scratch until the commit lands. Proposed: the route check in the hook judges only the staged route files and the indexes they change.
Would it have prevented this one: the draft in scratch, yes (it is how the entry came back); the check on staged paths, yes.

